    "acquired_at": "2026-11-13T17:30:12.305453+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-11-13T17:30:12.305453+00:00",
    "body": "NeoVolta, a U.S.-based energy technology company delivering scalable energy storage solutions, said its majority-owned subsidiary, NeoVolta Power, has entered into a $116-million master purchase agreement with a leading energy solutions provider.\nUnder the agreement announced November 13, NeoVolta Power will supply FEOC-compliant battery energy storage systems (BESS), with product deliveries scheduled for 2027. The agreement establishes a substantial base of contracted business, providing increased visibility into NeoVolta’s near-term manufacturing activity and supporting the company’s continued commercial expansion.\nThe purchase orders would provide a substantial foundation for NeoVolta’s manufacturing ramp in Pendergrass, Georgia, supporting increased production volumes as the company expands its domestic energy storage operations. As demand for FEOC-compliant domestic supply chains continue to grow, NeoVolta believes its U.S. manufacturing capabilities position the company to play an increasingly important role in the rapidly expanding energy storage market.\n“Securing this $116-million agreement represents a major milestone for NeoVolta, and we believe this is only the beginning of a much larger growth trajectory for our company,” said Ardes Johnson, CEO of NeoVolta. “As we scale production in Georgia and fulfill these commitments, we are building the foundation for rapid, sustained growth while positioning NeoVolta to meet the accelerating demand for domestically manufactured battery energy storage systems and become one of the leading U.S. suppliers in the industry.”\nNeoVolta is an innovator in energy storage solutions dedicated to advancing reliable, high-performance power infrastructure for residential, commercial, and utility applications. With a focus on scalable technology, domestic manufacturing, and strategic partnerships, NeoVolta is positioned to support the accelerating transition toward resilient energy systems.\n—This content was contributed by the communications team for NeoVolta .\nTagged in:\nbattery energy storage\nBESS\nbattery energy storage systems\nNeoVolta\nNeoVolta Power\nfinancial\nSept. 28—30, 2026\nWashington, D.C.\nRegister Now\nExplore this topic and more — live at Experience POWER. The power industry's most urgent decisions are being made right now. Be in the room where they happen.\nView Conference Program",
